<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles-Jacques Poncet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1698">1698</a>–<a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles-Jacques Poncet was a French physician working in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> who travelled through the Funj Sultanate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1698–1700 to treat the emperor Iyasu I. His account of the journey, published in 1704, gives one of the few European eyewitness descriptions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Sennar</a> at the height of the Funj sultanate, including its markets, court and trade.</p></div>
